//! Raw C interface of `sdk_glue.h` (sai-openbcm): the functions through which everything else
//! reaches the Broadcom SDK. `sdk_glue.c` stays C: it is the only file that includes SDK
//! headers and is compiled with the SDK's own defines.
//!
//! Declarations only: no `unsafe` block, no `unsafe impl`. The `unsafe extern "C"` block and
//! the `OB_E_*` constants are generated by `build.rs` from one table (name, C types), which
//! also writes the same declarations as C prototypes. When the header is around
//! (`SDK_GLUE_INC`, or `MDIO_SCRIPT_C_DIR` if `sdk_glue.h` is there) the target's C compiler
//! must accept those prototypes next to the header's (C refuses an incompatible
//! redeclaration) and every constant as a `_Static_assert`; [`HEADER_CHECK`] says what
//! happened, and `SDK_GLUE_SYS_CHECK=require` fails a build without the check.
//!
//! Why a table and not bindgen (the `sai-sys` recipe): the interface in use is six functions
//! over `int`, `unsigned` and `char*`, no struct crosses it, and the tool built on it should
//! not need libclang or the header to compile. When structs are bound (`ob_port_info_t`, ...),
//! their layout needs the checks `sai-sys` has: switch this crate to bindgen then.
//!
//! Since the switch bring-up was bound (ports, VLANs, link callback): 26 functions, and one
//! struct does cross, `ob_port_info_t` (four ints and a 16-byte name), with the two callback
//! types. Still the table: the struct is written out in `build.rs` with its size, alignment
//! and offsets asserted in Rust and, with the same numbers plus the field types, against the
//! header by the C compiler. A second struct is the point to move to bindgen.
//!
//! Nothing is linked by default. Feature `real` links the glue and libsdk (`SDK_GLUE_LINK`:
//! whitespace-separated `<path>/lib<name>.a`, `-L<dir>`, `-l<name>`); feature `fake` compiles
//! and links `fake/fake_glue.c`, which implements the same functions over an in-memory
//! register map driven by the "config file" it is given (format: the comment at its top).
//! Safe wrappers: the `sdk-glue` crate; nothing else should call these.
#![no_std]
#![allow(missing_docs, reason = "generated declarations; sdk_glue.h documents them")]

include!(concat!(env!("OUT_DIR"), "/bindings.rs"));

/// Outcome of the check of the generated declarations against `sdk_glue.h` in this build:
/// `checked <n> declarations with <cc> for <target> against <header>` or `skipped: <why>`.
pub const HEADER_CHECK: &str = env!("SDK_GLUE_SYS_CHECK_RESULT");

/// Which glue this build links: `real`, `fake` or `none`.
pub const LINKED: &str = env!("SDK_GLUE_SYS_LINKED");
